new file mode 100644
index 0000000..0650c60
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/routing.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,45 @@
+Feature: Routing and Persistence
+  As a user
+  I want to filter and persist my todos
+  So that I can organize my tasks across sessions
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded cleanly
+
+  Scenario: Default route is All
+    When the app loads
+    Then the "All" filter link has the class "selected"
+    And all todos are shown
+
+  Scenario: Active filter shows only active todos
+    Given a completed todo "Buy milk" exists and an active todo "Buy eggs" exists
+    When I click the "Active" filter link
+    Then only the active todo "Buy eggs" is visible in the list
+    And the "Active" filter link has the class "selected"
+
+  Scenario: Completed filter shows only completed todos
+    Given a completed todo "Buy milk" exists and an active todo "Buy eggs" exists
+    When I click the "Completed" filter link
+    Then only the completed todo "Buy milk" is visible in the list
+    And the "Completed" filter link has the class "selected"
+
+  Scenario: Persist todos to localStorage
+    Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
+    When the app triggers a save
+    Then localStorage has a key matching "todos-" with an entry for "Buy milk"
+
+  Scenario: Restore todos from localStorage on reload
+    Given localStorage contains a todo "Buy milk"
+    When the app reloads
+    Then the todo "Buy milk" appears in the list
+
+  Scenario: Active filter persists on reload
+    Given the "Active" filter is selected
+    When the app reloads
+    Then the "Active" filter link still has the class "selected"
+
+  Scenario: Toggle in filtered view hides item
+    Given a completed todo "Buy milk" exists and an active todo "Buy eggs" exists
+    When I click the "Active" filter
+    And I mark "Buy eggs" as completed
+    Then "Buy eggs" is hidden from the list
\ No newline at end of file
diff --git a/features/todo-management.feature b/features/todo-management.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..5862904
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/todo-management.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,109 @@
+Feature: Todo Management
+  As a user
+  I want to manage a todo list
+  So that I can track my tasks
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded cleanly
+
+  Scenario: Create a new todo
+    Given no todos exist
+    When I type "Buy milk" into the new-todo input and press Enter
+    Then a todo item with title "Buy milk" appears in the list
+    And the new-todo input is cleared
+
+  Scenario: Reject empty or whitespace-only todos
+    When I type "   " into the new-todo input and press Enter
+    Then no todo item is added to the list
+    And the todo list remains empty
+
+  Scenario: Toggle a todo as completed
+    Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
+    When I click the toggle checkbox on the todo
+    Then the todo item has the class "completed"
+    And its toggle checkbox becomes checked
+
+  Scenario: Toggle a completed todo back to active
+    Given a completed todo "Buy milk" exists
+    When I click the toggle checkbox on the todo
+    Then the todo item does not have the class "completed"
+    And its toggle checkbox is unchecked
+
+  Scenario: Delete a todo
+    Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
+    When I click the destroy button on the todo
+    Then the todo "Buy milk" is removed from the list
+
+  Scenario: Activate editing mode on double-click
+    Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
+    When I double-click the label of the todo
+    Then the todo item has the class "editing"
+    And the edit input is focused
+
+  Scenario: Save edited todo on Enter
+    Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
+    When I double-click the label and change the value to "Buy eggs" and press Enter
+    Then the todo title is "Buy eggs"
+    And the todo item does not have the class "editing"
+
+  Scenario: Save edited todo on blur
+    Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
+    When I double-click the label and change the value to "Buy eggs" and blur the input
+    Then the todo title is "Buy eggs"
+    And the todo item does not have the class "editing"
+
+  Scenario: Destroy todo on empty edit
+    Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
+    When I double-click the label and clear the input and press Enter
+    Then the todo "Buy milk" is removed from the list
+
+  Scenario: Discard edit on Escape
+    Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
+    When I double-click the label and press Escape
+    Then the todo title remains "Buy milk"
+    And the todo item does not have the class "editing"
+
+  Scenario: Mark all todos as complete
+    Given todos "Buy milk" and "Buy eggs" exist
+    When I click the toggle-all checkbox
+    Then all todos have the class "completed"
+
+  Scenario: Unmark all todos when toggle-all is unchecked
+    Given all todos are marked completed
+    When I click the toggle-all checkbox
+    Then no todos have the class "completed"
+
+  Scenario: Hide main and footer when no todos
+    When no todos exist
+    Then the #main section is hidden
+    And the #footer section is hidden
+
+  Scenario: Show main and footer when todos exist
+    Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
+    Then the #main section is visible
+    And the #footer section is visible
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed todos
+    Given a completed todo "Buy milk" exists and an active todo "Buy eggs" exists
+    When I click the clear-completed button
+    Then only the todo "Buy eggs" remains in the list
+    And the clear-completed button is hidden
+
+  Scenario: Pluralized item count - zero items
+    Given no todos exist
+    Then the todo-count shows "0 items left"
+
+  Scenario: Pluralized item count - one item
+    Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
+    Then the todo-count shows "1 item left"
+
+  Scenario: Pluralized item count - two items
+    Given todos "Buy milk" and "Buy eggs" exist
+    Then the todo-count shows "2 items left"
+
+  Scenario: Toggle-all checkbox reflects individual toggles
+    Given todos "Buy milk" and "Buy eggs" exist
+    When I mark "Buy milk" as completed
+    Then the toggle-all checkbox is unchecked
+    When I mark "Buy eggs" as completed
+    Then the toggle-all checkbox is checked
